{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Take heed.</b> Every angel does the word of HaShem, neither adding nor diminishing. Thus Satan in Job was an angel, and thus the one who went out to meet Balaam, as an adversary to him. And behold, the one who heeds the voice of the angel is heeding the voice of the honored Name." "<b>And the word אל תמר בו [do not rebel against him].</b> It is difficult. Now the reason appears to be like וימרו בי [they rebelled against Me] (Ezekiel 20:8), except that it should have been תמרה; therefore the sages of Spain needed to say that בו is of the piel-doubling pattern, on the model of ויסב אלהים את העם [and Elohim led the people around] (above 13:18), for the entire paradigm is of the piel-doubling pattern. For ורחבה ונסבה [it was broad and it curved] (Ezekiel 41:7) is nifal-pattern, like ונבלה שם [let its name be confounded] (Genesis 11:7) from the root בלל, and נבקה רוח מצרים [the spirit of Egypt shall be emptied] (Isaiah 19:3) from the root בוקק (ibid. 24:1). And do not marvel that these are two roots yet the meaning is one, for behold שורר בביתו [he rules in his house] (Esther 1:22) is like כי שרית עם אלהים [for you have striven with Elohim] (Genesis 32:29), and similar is אל תמר בו. And ממר ליולדתו [a rebellious son to his mother] (Proverbs 17:25) is on the pattern of מכס [tax] (Numbers 31:28), which is from the root of תכוסו על השה [you shall count for the lamb] (above 12:4), of the piel-doubling pattern." "And know that <b>for My name is within him</b> is joined with 'take heed before him and heed his voice,' like ואף לאמתך תעשה כן [and also to your maidservant you shall do thus] (Deuteronomy 15:17). And I have already explained that the honored Name is the name of the essence, for He alone is, and the attribute of the Name is also found, for He is all and from Him is all." "<b>And the meaning of 'within him.'</b> A parable of a sphere, where the point is near to every extremity. Therefore the glory of HaShem was within the camp, and journeyed within the camps. And so it is written כי אתה ה' בקרב העם הזה [for you, YHWH, are in the midst of this people] (Numbers 14:14), and it is written ויוצר רוח אדם בקרבו [who forms the spirit of man within him] (Zechariah 12:1). And do not wonder that it is written כי אם שמוע תשמע בקולו [but pay attention to heed his voice] and afterward ועשית כל אשר אדבר [and you shall do all that I speak]. And behold I will give you a parable. All scholars of measurements have brought conclusive proofs that the essence of the moon is a body that receives the light of the sun, for it has no luminescence of itself. And because of this the sun is darkened when the moon conjoins with it by day, and both are in spheres resembling the sphere of the constellations. The darkening is only that the moon enters beneath the sun, and both are spherical. Now the face of the moon that is toward the sun is all light, and its face that is above it is darkness and not light. And the light of the sun is hidden even at new moon, when the shadow of the earth enters between the sun and the moon — no light remains to the moon. Now we know that the light of the moon at night illuminates the air. So if Reuben says 'this is the light of the moon,' he speaks truth, and if Simeon says 'this is the light of the sun,' he speaks truth."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:56.139298305Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}